From: At30c <At30c@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] radio: shorten the Bluetooth host wake and Wi-Fi rx wakelocks

With the screen off the y2slte stayed awake about a third of the time,
almost all of it in radio wakelocks: BT_host_wake (606 wakeups, 2.7 s on
average each) and wlan_rx_wake (1235 wakeups, 0.9 s each) in about 1.5 h.
The work behind each wakeup takes milliseconds; the rest is the timed
wakelock the drivers keep so that the upper layers can take theirs.

Keep it for 250 ms instead of 1 s after the Bluetooth chip deasserts
host wake (bcm43xx), and for 200 ms instead of 500 ms after each received
Wi-Fi packet (bcmdhd 101_16, DHD_PACKET_TIMEOUT_MS). The Bluetooth stack
and the network stack take their own wakelocks while they process the
data. Transmit and control wakelocks are unchanged.
---
diff --git a/drivers/bluetooth/bcm43xx.c b/drivers/bluetooth/bcm43xx.c
index c6e828e..bb0876b 100644
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/bcm43xx.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/bcm43xx.c
@@ -189,10 +189,13 @@ static void update_host_wake_locked(int host_wake)
 	} else  {
 		/* Take a timed wakelock, so that upper layers can take it.
 		 * The chipset deasserts the hostwake lock, when there is no
-		 * more data to send.
+		 * more data to send. The Bluetooth stack takes its own wakelock
+		 * while it handles the data; 250 ms instead of 1 s, since each
+		 * of the frequent wearable/BLE wakeups kept the device awake for
+		 * the whole second (2.7 s on average per host wake).
 		 */
-		pr_info("[BT] update_host_wake_locked host_wake is deasserted. release wakelock in 1s\n");
-		wake_lock_timeout(&bt_lpm.host_wake_lock, HZ);
+		pr_info("[BT] update_host_wake_locked host_wake is deasserted. release wakelock in 250ms\n");
+		wake_lock_timeout(&bt_lpm.host_wake_lock, msecs_to_jiffies(250));
 
         if (bt_lpm.dev_wake == 0)
             exynos_update_ip_idle_status(idle_btip_index, STATUS_IDLE);
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/bcmdhd_101_16/dhd.h b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/bcmdhd_101_16/dhd.h
index cc487ce..0c6eb1f 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/bcmdhd_101_16/dhd.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/bcmdhd_101_16/dhd.h
@@ -1920,7 +1920,12 @@ extern void dhd_os_oob_irq_wake_unlock(dhd_pub_t *pub);
 #define DHD_OS_OOB_IRQ_WAKE_UNLOCK(pub)			dhd_os_oob_irq_wake_unlock(pub)
 #endif /* BCMPCIE_OOB_HOST_WAKE */
 
-#define DHD_PACKET_TIMEOUT_MS	500
+/*
+ * Wakelock held after each received packet so that the network stack and
+ * the app can take theirs: 200 ms instead of 500 ms (0.9 s on average per
+ * rx wake on the y2slte with the screen off).
+ */
+#define DHD_PACKET_TIMEOUT_MS	200
 #define DHD_EVENT_TIMEOUT_MS	1500
 #define SCAN_WAKE_LOCK_TIMEOUT	10000
 #define MAX_TX_TIMEOUT			500
